  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>If two tangents drawn from a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> to the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> are at right angles.</p><p>Given the equation of parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Then, the locus point is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math></p><p>Locus is directrix of parabola is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>"
